  exe_cli_errors_args.pcpp - Build-kind compliance: program arguments without -r

  Everything after -- is the program's, so it needs a run (-r or -d): exit 2
  and the hint to run pcpp -h.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\exe_build_run.pcpp -- x
  EXPECT:
    PaskalCPP™ CLI v<VERSION>
    Copyright © 2026-present tinyBigGAMES™ LLC, All Rights Reserved.
    https://paskalcpp.org

    Error: -- (program arguments) is used with -r or -d only

    Run pcpp -h to see available options
  EXITCODE: 2
  <VERSION> is the compiler's version (the banner's one changing text); the
  tester runs pcpp.exe itself (cmCli), once: the CLI is the same for every
  target. This file is not compiled.
*******************************************************************************/

